You review the protocol of one registered clinical trial as a trial methodologist, before its results exist (imagine it is {{ as_of }}). Use the registry text; general methodological knowledge is allowed, knowledge of this trial's result is not. For every factor give a level and, where the text supports it, one short phrase copied exactly from the text (else "").

Registry text:
<<<TRIAL
{{ text }}
TRIAL>>>

Factors:
1. endpoint_snr: is the primary outcome objective and sensitive enough to show the intended effect in this trial? "high" (objective measurement, sensitive to the mechanism), "medium", "low" (subjective, insensitive, or a ceiling/floor is likely).
2. add_on_ceiling: does the control or background care already produce much of the improvement, leaving little room for an added effect? "yes", "no", "unclear".
3. time_window: is the duration of exposure and follow-up long enough for the expected biological response? "adequate", "short", "unclear".
4. power_realism: is the planned sample size adequate for a clinically meaningful difference on this endpoint, given its usual variability? "adequate", "underpowered", "unclear".
5. population_enrichment: are participants selected for the target or deficit the intervention acts on (rather than a heterogeneous population)? "enriched", "heterogeneous", "unclear".
6. delivery: can the intervention reach the target at an effective, safe exposure in these participants? "likely", "doubtful", "not_applicable" (behavioural or device interventions acting directly), "unclear".
7. bias_room: how much room for bias does the design leave (blinding, control type, outcome assessment)? "low", "some", "high".

